Here's how you can implement this in Java:

```java
public class PowerOfThreeChecker {
    public static boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        // The largest power of 3 within the 32-bit signed integer range
        int maxPowerOfThree = 1162261467; // 3^19

        // Check if n is positive and if maxPowerOfThree is divisible by n
        return n > 0 && maxPowerOfThree % n == 0;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(27)); // true
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(0));  // false
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(-1)); // false
    }
}
```

This solution works because any power of three will divide the largest power of three exactly, provided it is within the valid range. This method avoids the need for iterative or recursive checks, making it both concise and efficient.

